        "abstract": "I am truly honored and delighted to serve as the Vice President (VP) for Education of the IEEE Computational Intelligence Society (CIS). Education is a cornerstone of shaping individuals and societies, which fuels personal growth, drives technological innovation, and promotes societal advancement. IEEE CIS recognizes this importance and places education at the core of its mission, empowering students and professionals through diverse educational opportunities in computational intelligence (CI). With the opportunity to serve in this pivotal role, I aim to build on the achievements of past VPs for Education to continue pursuing excellence. My focus will be on enhancing educational resources and portals, incorporating modern educational trends into our programs and activities, and addressing the needs of both learners and educators.",
