        "abstract": "As you might know, the IEEE Computational Intelligence Society (IEEE CIS) rooted from the IEEE Neural Network Council established in 1990, which was transited to the IEEE Neural Network Society in 2002. Finally, the name of the society was changed to IEEE CIS in 2004. Interestingly, however, the first IEEE World Congress on Computational Intelligence (WCCI) was held in 1994 in Orlando, Florida, USA. And to my surprise, I recently found that I published a paper titled “Fuzzy linearization for nonlinear system: a preliminary study” in FUZZ-IEEE’1994, which was part of WCCI’1994. Unfortunately, I was not able to attend the conference in person, mainly because it was hardly possible for a PhD student in China at that time to afford the cost to attend a conference held in the US.",
