                "firstName": "Chuan-Kang",
                "lastName": "Ting"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "Artificial Intelligence (AI) has emerged as a transformative technology powering innovations that impact industries, societies, and individuals alike. At the core of this progress, Computational Intelligence (CI) plays a pivotal role in advancing AI's capabilities by enabling complex problem-solving approaches that incorporate knowledge, adaptability, and computational paradigms. This impact is clearly evident in IEEE Computational Intelligence Society (CIS) publications, which consistently showcase high-quality, impactful research that drives the development of AI. IEEE CIS's Transactions—TNNLS, TFS, TEVC, TOG, TCDS, TETCI, and TAI—along with our dedicated Computational Intelligence Magazine (CIM), provide a vital platform for groundbreaking research and thought leadership. This success stands as a testament to the quality and relevance of the work published and to the dedication of our research community, which continues to push the boundaries of AI.",
